<title>DENMARK: Danish Nov North Sea gas production rises 4.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Danish Nov North Sea gas production rises 4.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish Underground Consortium (DUC) North Sea natural gas production rose 4.5 percent to 554 million cubic metres in November from 530 million cubic metres in October, a spokesman for operator A.P. Moeller Group said on Thursday.</p>
<p>    (Million cubic metres)   Nov 96    Oct 96   Nov 95</p>
<p>    Total production	    554	  530	471</p>
<p>DUC is responsible for virtually the entire output from Denmark's North Sea oil and gas fields which make the country the third-biggest producer in western Europe after Norway and Britain.</p>
<p>A.P. Moeller Group owns 39 percent of DUC. Its two partners, Royal Dutch/Shell group and Texaco Inc own 46 percent and 15 percent respectively.</p>
<p>-- Chris Follett, Copenhagen Newsroom +45-33-969656</p>
</text>
